        &nbsp;<a href="post.asp?ARCHIVE=&method=TopicQuote&TOPIC_ID=7917&FORUM_ID=14&CAT_ID=6&Forum_Title=New+Adventures+%2D+General+Board&Topic_Title=CoH%3A+Trick+or+Treat%21"><img src="icon_reply_topic.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Reply with Quote" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>

        <hr noshade size="1">
        
<font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> So last night on Test Server there were TONS of people for the Paragon City Council (PCC) event... it didn't last long (20 min or so) but it was pretty fun while it lasted.  CuppaJo (admin/moderator from the forums) told everyone they had 20 minutes to run around clicking mission doors, looking for "clues"...</P><P>Basically, if you clicked on a mission door you either got:</P><P>(a) a big flash of TREAT (like the CLUE flash) and you got either an inspiration, an enhancement, or a temp power that let you throw a rock.</P><P>or</P><P>(b) a big flash of TRICK, and the door would OPEN and monsters would emerge!  I personally saw "zombies" (Banished Pantheon human-sized husk models, except without the WWII attire or weapons)... "pumpkin-heads" (Devoured Earth razorvine model except with PUMPKIN HEADS!)... and "witches" which I only saw after someone had defeated them, so I didn't get a good look.</P><P>All in all it was pretty fun, "trick or treating"... it was just a twenty minute "preview" for this weekend's upcoming BIG event.</P><P>Oh, they also made it night time... not sure if they increased the fog or not --- certainly wasn't as bad as Dark Astoria.  I wasn't even sure they had made it night, except when the 20 min session was over, they CLICK turned on the sun again. <img src=icon_smile_big.gif border=0 align=middle></P><P>Lots of cries as people's retinas were seared by the sudden light.  </P><P>Also, something you don't notice while it's gone but only when it comes back... the individual "neighborhood" music tracks that play as you move around the city were shut off during the event and only came on when they turned the world "normal" again.</P><P>If I can remember tonight, I'll post the few screenshots I managed to get.</P><P>Brax</P><P></P><P></P><P>Edited by - Braxzana on 11/02/2004  22:25:39</font> 

